    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nMini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nI use Colemak keyboard layout, so I always map k to i when I use neovim/vim,\r\nusing k for insert and inside operator prepend.\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.82\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. my keymaps\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"\", \"k\", \"i\")\r\n```\r\n2. set inside = \"k\" when I setup mini.ai\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    -- Main textobject prefixes\r\n    around = 'a',\r\n    inside = 'k',\r\n\r\n    -- Next/last variants\r\n    around_next = 'ae',\r\n    inside_next = 'ke',\r\n    around_last = 'au',\r\n    inside_last = 'ku',\r\n }\r\n})\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWorks both mini.ai keymaps and my own keymaps\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIt works when I type `ckf`, but not works when I type `ckw`.\r\nI read Mini.ai source code, I think, mini.ai overwrote my mapping for 'k'.",
