            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue! Never really looked into different keyboard layouts, so didn't think about this use case.\r\n\r\n> I read Mini.ai source code, I think, mini.ai overwrote my mapping for 'k'.\r\n\r\nOverriding mappings for `a` and `i` is the whole point of this plugin. The issue here is that `iw` is not a 'mini.ai'-defined textobject, so it falls back to being equivalent to typing `iw`, which is not correct in your user case.\r\n\r\nI'll see what I can do here.",
