            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I tried this solution.\r\n1. I mapped \"i\" to \"l\", because I need to use \"i\" to move the cursor to the right.\r\n2. I use `vim.o.langmap = 'k;i,i;k'`\r\n\"i\" will move the cursor up\r\n\r\n3. Modify langmap to `vim.o.langmap = 'k;i'`\r\n\"i\" moves the cursor to the right, but \"k\" doesn't go into insert mode, \"k\" also moves the cursor to the right\r\n\r\nadd keymap: `vim.keymap.set({ \"n\", \"x\", \"o\" }, \"k\", \"i\")`\r\n\"k\" still can't get into insert mode",
