            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I tried this solution.\r\n> ...\r\n>     2. I use `vim.o.langmap = 'k;i,i;k'`\r\n>        \"i\" will move the cursor up\r\n\r\nSorry, I do not understand the problem here. With `vim.o.langmap = 'ki,ik'` keys \"i\" and \"k\" are essentially swapped: use \"i\" to go up and \"k\" for all \"regular\" \"inside\" textobjects (like `vk)`, `dkw`, etc.). This works and does not need any more additional mappings.",
