        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "The problem is that colemak's i is qwerty's l, and I need to keep the neovim convention, so I need to map i to l.\r\nAt the same time, I needed a key instead of i, for entering insert mode and text objects, and I chose the k key.\r\nThe current mapping situation is as follows:\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set({ \"n\", \"x\" }, \"i\", \"l\")\r\nvim.keymap.set({ \"n\", \"x\", \"o\" }, \"k\", \"i\")\r\n```\r\nSo my scenario involves three keys, i, l, k, and I cannot simply swap k and i.\r\nThe implementation principle of mini.ai is to remap inside, which will theoretically conflict with my keys.\r\nMaybe only compatible from within.",
            "created_at": "2024-05-14T14:07:01Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/195#issuecomment-2110339250",
